sequenceDiagram
  autonumber
  participant A as Browser A (client-core)
  participant IDB as IndexedDB
  participant G as Gateway
  participant O as Owner (BoardActor)
  participant PG as Postgres
  participant R as Redis Pub/Sub
  participant B as Browser B
  A->>A: stamp op (HLC tick), plan<br/>keys
  A->>IDB: append op to the log
  IDB-->>A: durable
  A->>A: show it (optimistic view)
  A->>G: OP (paced: 20/s, burst 50)
  G->>G: rate limit, then queue (one<br/>request at a time per<br/>connection)
  G->>O: forward (owner from 5s cache<br/>/ Redis)
  O->>O: dedup (LRU), validate shape,<br/>role, clock, references
  O->>O: add to batch (5 ms window)
  O->>PG: one transaction: drop known<br/>op_ids, UPDATE ... WHERE<br/>fence = :fence, INSERT ops
  PG-->>O: COMMIT ok (versions)
  O->>O: apply to memory
  O-->>G: OP_ACK {op_id, version}
  G-->>A: OP_ACK, op leaves the queue
  O->>R: PUBLISH board:id {op,<br/>version}
  R-->>G: message
  G-->>B: OP_BROADCAST
  B->>B: merge, render ("moved by" if<br/>B's own move lost)
